  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Most of the time I'll get 60fps fine, but the app will occasionally drop to 1 fps or less for multiple seconds at a time, then inexplicably recover some time later.\n\nNot even sure what to do to cause this, but it seems like manually setting a framerate cap instead of VSync makes it happen more frequently\n\nHave tried disabling app battery optimizations, disabling power saver, using a charger, setting phone to performance mode, disabling virtual memory, etc. with no change.\n\nEdit: Got it on video – https://youtu.be/Qm0XIsiQMEk\n\nEdit 2: Still happens after disabling virtual memory – https://youtu.be/Og2BUYi2HmM\n\nOS: Android 12 / OneUI4.1 \n\nCPU: Snapdragon 855 / Kryo 485 \n\nGPU: Adreno 640\n\nRAM: 6GB Physical + 6GB Virtual",
